p.src:
The canonical momenta are defined by the Lagrangian, not by a guess based on a single particle velocity: $\begin{aligned}
  p_X&=\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot X}
      =M\dot X+m(\dot X+\dot x),
      \\
  p_x&=\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot x}
      =m(\dot X+\dot x)+m\dot x.
      \end{aligned}$ The first expression is the ordinary total horizontal momentum: the wedge contributes $M\dot X$, and the particle contributes $m(\dot X+\dot x)$. It appears here as the momentum conjugate to the coordinate $X$.

